# Markdown must be stored with LF. A CRLF-terminated `---` fence stops GitHub's
# YAML front-matter parser from finding the closing delimiter, so it swallows the
# entire document into the front-matter table and renders it as one wall of text.
*.md text eol=lf

# The model viewer downloads these from raw.githubusercontent.com and checks each
# one against the sha256 in manifest.json. raw serves the blob as git stores it,
# while `xi mv update` hashes the working copy — so under core.autocrlf those are
# two different byte streams and every list fails verification on every client,
# forever. Pin them to LF so the working copy, the blob and what raw serves are
# the same bytes.
mv/lists/*.json text eol=lf
